186481634 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "da46d0be-42c1-57a1-ab4a-e8a9512a5cad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481646 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481646 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481646 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee2dac8c-ea1a-540c-93ab-6f8d5b85be8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186481588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "287256f7-b082-5a2a-854b-414b7b8a37a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186481653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162827" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.16$ | $0.09$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.44$ | $0.21$ | $0.05$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=0,Y=0)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=0)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "34f7a331-3a09-5214-b793-a1233bb14dc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1074 "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=0)=f(0,0)=0.09.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=0)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(0)=0.3\\cdot 0.3=0.09.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,-2) & =0.16\\ne 0.3\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491606 #edb/ref 1080 "0.42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491606 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491606 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50e2ab1f-ce9b-5969-b153-8c952635697f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491647 #edb/ref 1080 "Impossible to determine using the given information." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491647 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491647 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c01961e-283c-5e82-89cd-af921b8b18cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491665 #edb/ref 1080 "0.06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491665 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491665 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "79b00643-d756-5605-96ea-7aef73ff16fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491785 #edb/ref 1080 "0.28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491785 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491785 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bfceb24c-fc28-5771-a384-73a046579e6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491873 #edb/ref 1080 "0.09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491873 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491873 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f4eeb262-2789-575f-8f08-0e1aa6046842" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186491606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186491647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186491665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186491785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186491873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186491647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186491918 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5826e975-df63-51e0-a67a-1164fd2d1f8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492011 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759